id: pm-s4y3z4
title: "The docs gate enforces link resolution but not doc reachability, so orphaned docs pass CI and the advertised docs map silently drifts"
description: "docs-skills-gate.mjs validates that relative markdown links resolve, but has no inverse check for docs nothing links to. docs/PR_REVIEW_LOOP.md has zero inbound links repo-wide; docs/PERFORMANCE.md and docs/RELATIONSHIP_GRAPH.md are absent from docs/README.md, the file AGENTS.md advertises as the full docs map."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[5]: agent-ux,ci-gate,docs,progressive-disclosure,repo-organization
created_at: "2026-07-26T18:28:37.877Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:32.338Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:31.786Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:31.786Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The docs gate fails when a docs/*.md file is not reachable from docs/README.md, directly or transitively; An explicit opt-out list covers deliberately standalone docs so the gate is narrowed rather than silenced; docs/PR_REVIEW_LOOP.md, docs/PERFORMANCE.md and docs/RELATIONSHIP_GRAPH.md are each linked, opted out, or removed"
goal: project management = context management
value: "Keeps the advertised progressive-disclosure map and the on-disk docs tree in agreement automatically, instead of after each manual audit."
impact: Under a progressive-disclosure navigation model an unlinked doc is invisible to the agent it was written for while still costing review and maintenance.
outcome: "A reachability pass in the docs gate with an explicit opt-out list, and the three current orphans linked, listed, or removed."
why_now: pm-c97q closed the same class by hand-adding two links and added no enforcement; the class has already recurred with three different files.
parent: pm-kb5h
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Enforced transitive documentation reachability with explicit reasoned exceptions and connected eight previously unreachable pages. Image embeds retain existence checks but cannot establish navigation reachability.
expected_result: Every documentation page is reachable from the index or has a validated individual exception; disconnected cycles fail.
actual_result: Full and links-only documentation gates pass with an empty exception list; seeded disconnected-cycle and invalid-exception regressions pass. Image-only orphan and malformed-image URL negative controls pass; fixture fallback is isolated.
