comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T09:19:20.059Z","harness:codex","Fresh documentation topology evidence 2026-08-04: the tracked docs tree contains 75 files; docs/SDK.md alone is 3,182 lines and docs/COMMANDS.md 1,095 lines. The docs/skills freshness and link/content gate passes, but that does not establish reachability from the advertised docs map or prevent concept duplication across large reference documents. This item remains the canonical reachability owner."
  "2026-08-16T10:37:55.529Z","harness:claude-code","Precedent for the reachability half of this chore: docs-skills-gate.mjs now has validateSkillReferenceReachability, which fails when a file under .agents/skills/<skill>/references is not linked from that skill's SKILL.md. It reuses the existing extractRelativeMarkdownLinks + resolveMarkdownLink pair, so the docs/ direction needs the same two calls against the docs map rather than new machinery. Negative control proven: an unlinked references/ORPHAN.md fails the gate naming the exact path; removing it restores the pass. Shipped under pm-f6zjpq."
  "2026-09-05T17:53:11.394Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: 8457 tests across 617 files pass at exact 100% lines/statements/functions/branches (60094/62503/12956/47351 covered). Full quality:static passes, including unchanged token ceilings, docstrings, graph composition, and record integrity. Typecheck, version policy, ShellCheck, credential scan, zero-vulnerability dependency audit, and enforced Trivy scan pass. Final npm/npx and Bun/bunx packed smoke covers all 13 packages; separate temporary installed SDK/CLI acceptance passes. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero blocking Sentry groups and no failures lacking error codes. PR review and hosted checks are the remaining delivery stage."
  "2026-09-05T18:11:33.221Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1204 identifies image-only reachability, unquoted HTML anchors, and test fixture fallback. CodeQL alert 38 flags regex HTML stripping in heading extraction; no executable HTML sink exists, but a maintained HTML parser will remove the fragile step. Add negative controls before implementation; retain existing coverage and gate thresholds."
  "2026-09-05T18:18:55.097Z","harness:codex","PR #1204 accepted feedback: images remain checked for file existence and malformed URLs, but only navigation links establish documentation reachability. A Markdown file referenced only as an image remains unreachable. Corrected the test filesystem adapter so the exception registry is isolated for both supplied and actual-reader fallback paths."
  "2026-09-05T18:34:31.275Z","harness:codex","PR #1204 round-one dispositions recorded on every original review/comment surface with up/down reactions. Three documentation/test findings fixed; two unsupported findings answered with source and tracker evidence. Regex heading stripping removed after CodeQL alert 38; hosted revalidation remains pending on the next head. Final local proof: 8458 tests in 617 files, exact coverage 60107/60107 lines, 62520/62520 statements, 12957/12957 functions, 47365/47365 branches. All 68 touched named non-test functions have declaration JSDoc. Full static/type/documentation gates, all five PM-linked runs, final npm/npx+Bun/bunx 13-package smoke, separate temporary packed acceptance, dependency audit, and immutable tracked-tree Trivy scan pass. Sourcery substantive review is unavailable under its current quota; Greptile has not responded. These are availability limitations, not approval."
